## 3. Component Architecture

- [ ] **3.1** Interactive elements use Shadcn primitives from `@/components/ui/*` — `Button`, `Card`, `Dialog`, `Badge`, `Tabs`, `Table`, `Select`, `Input`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`
- [ ] **3.2** **Props before overrides** — if a Shadcn component has a built-in prop for the need (`size="sm"`, `variant="outline"`, `icon={<Icon />}`), use it and delete the equivalent custom Tailwind classes.

  **The `!` important modifier is a signal that this check was skipped.** `size-16!` on an `Avatar` says a plain `size-16` lost a specificity fight, and reaching for `!` settles the symptom while leaving the cause. Find the cause first: the component may have a prop for it; the class may be colliding with one the component already applies, in which case `cn()` merging should win and something is bypassing it; or the value may belong in the variant file under **3.4**. `!` is acceptable only against a third-party stylesheet you cannot edit — never against a Shadcn primitive in this repo, where you own both sides
- [ ] **3.3** No new wrapper components (`ThemedButton`, `ThemedBadge`) — compose Shadcn primitives with explicit Tailwind classes
- [ ] **3.4** **The component's own file is the entire edit surface.** `components/ui/` files are **not modified** — customization goes in `components/uiable/` variant files. The same applies to everything else outside the component under review: `src/app/globals.css`, `tailwind.config.*`, `tsconfig.json`, `eslint.config.mjs`, `package.json`, other blocks, and shared helpers are all **read-only** while fixing a finding.

  The reason is blast radius. Retuning a token in `globals.css` to fix one component's contrast silently restyles every other component and block in the library, and nobody notices until an unrelated review fails. One finding is never worth a library-wide change made without looking at the library.

  **When a fix genuinely requires an out-of-scope change, stop and report it — do not work around it.** The workaround is always available and always wrong: hardcode the value and the check passes, but you have traded a scope violation for a **2.4** / **11.6** violation and shipped something that breaks the moment a buyer changes their theme (`block-audit` **7.1**). Emit 🔴 FAIL naming the check, the file that would need to change, and what change it needs. That is a design-system decision, and handing it over intact is the correct outcome rather than a failure of the review
- [ ] **3.5** Component is declared **and exported in one statement**. Both a trailing default export and an arrow assignment are rejected:

  ```tsx
  export default function ComponentName() { ... }   // ✅

  function ComponentName() { ... }                  // ❌ trailing export
  export default ComponentName

  const ComponentName = () => { ... }               // ❌ arrow assignment
  export default ComponentName
  ```

- [ ] **3.6** Section comment is present above the export — exact format and naming rules in **10.6**
- [ ] **3.7** **Named interface once a component has more than two props (CRITICAL)** — applies to the main component and every sub-component (**3.9**) alike. At one or two props, typing inline on the destructure is acceptable. At three or more, a named interface is mandatory, declared above the component alongside the other types (**1.2**):

  ```tsx
  function UserBadge({ name, role }: { name: string; role: string }) { ... }   // ✅ 2 props, inline is fine

  interface UserCardProps {
    name: string
    role: string
    avatarUrl: string
  }

  function UserCard({ name, role, avatarUrl }: UserCardProps) { ... }         // ✅ 3 props, named interface

  function UserCard({
    name,
    role,
    avatarUrl,
  }: {
    name: string
    role: string
    avatarUrl: string
  }) { ... }                                                                 // ❌ 3 props, still typed inline
  ```

- [ ] **3.8** Self-contained and portable — no Redux/Zustand dependency unless explicitly part of the app layer
- [ ] **3.9** **Extract reusable sub-components (CRITICAL)** — actively judge whether part of the JSX should become its own component. Candidates: anything repeated, anything rendered inside `.map()`, and any self-contained chunk big enough to hide the parent's structure. When one exists, extract it as a **normal `function` declaration above the main component, in the same file**. If it takes more than two props, its interface is named and goes at the top with the other types, same as the main component (**1.2**, **3.7**):

  ```tsx
  interface FeatureCardProps {
    title: string
    icon: ReactNode
    description: string
  }

  function FeatureCard({ title, icon, description }: FeatureCardProps) { ... }

  export default function FeatureSection() {
    return <div>{features.map((f) => <FeatureCard key={f.id} {...f} />)}</div>
  }
  ```

  Three ways to get this wrong:

  ```tsx
  {features.map((f) => <div key={f.id}>{/* 50 lines */}</div>)}         // ❌ left inline
  const FeatureCard = ({ title }: FeatureCardProps) => { ... }          // ❌ arrow — see 1.5
  function FeatureCard({ title, icon, description }: { title: string; icon: ReactNode; description: string }) { ... }  // ❌ 3 props, still inline — see 3.7
  import { FeatureCard } from "./feature-card"                          // ❌ separate file
  ```

  A sub-component used only by this component never gets its own file. The sole exception is a block already large enough to justify a `components/` subfolder — the same carve-out as **1.3**/**1.4**.

- [ ] **3.10** **Components over raw HTML** — before writing a raw element, check this table for an equivalent. Raw HTML is fine only when nothing here fits, or the element is semantically required (`<section>`, `<nav>`, `<ul>`, `<article>`, `<h2>`).

  **Direct swaps — raw element → component**

  | Raw HTML | Component | Import from `@/components/ui/…` |
  | :------- | :-------- | :------------------------------ |
  | `<button>` | `Button` | `button` |
  | `<a>` styled as a button | `Button asChild` | `button` |
  | several buttons in a row | `ButtonGroup` | `button-group` |
  | `<input>` | `Input` | `input` |
  | `<input>` with a prefix/suffix addon | `InputGroup` | `input-group` |
  | `<input type="checkbox">` | `Checkbox` | `checkbox` |
  | `<input type="checkbox">` as an on/off control | `Switch` | `switch` |
  | `<input type="radio">` | `RadioGroup`, `RadioGroupItem` | `radio-group` |
  | `<input type="range">` | `Slider` | `slider` |
  | `<input type="date">` | `Calendar` | `calendar` |
  | one-time-code inputs | `InputOTP` | `input-otp` |
  | `<textarea>` | `Textarea` | `textarea` |
  | `<select>` | `Select` and its parts | `select` |
  | `<label>` | `Label` | `label` |
  | `<form>` | `Form` and its parts | `form` |
  | `<fieldset>` / a label+input+error group | `Field`, `FieldSet` | `field` |
  | `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tr>`, `<th>`, `<td>` | `Table`, `TableHeader`, `TableBody`, `TableRow`, `TableHead`, `TableCell` | `table` |
  | `<hr>`, or `<br>` used as a divider | `Separator` | `separator` |
  | `<details>` / `<summary>` | `Accordion`, or `Collapsible` for one | `accordion`, `collapsible` |
  | `<dialog>` | `Dialog`; `AlertDialog` to confirm; `Sheet` side panel; `Drawer` on mobile | `dialog`, `alert-dialog`, `sheet`, `drawer` |
  | `<progress>` | `Progress` | `progress` |
  | `<kbd>` | `Kbd` | `kbd` |
  | `<img>` that must hold a ratio | `AspectRatio` | `aspect-ratio` |
  | avatar `<img>` with initials fallback | `Avatar`, `AvatarImage`, `AvatarFallback` | `avatar` |
  | `<span>` as a tag, chip or pill | `Badge` | `badge` |
  | `<div>` as a card | `Card`, `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter` | `card` |
  | `<nav>` of ancestor links | `Breadcrumb` | `breadcrumb` |
  | `<nav>` of page numbers | `Pagination` | `pagination` |
  | `<nav>` site navigation | `NavigationMenu`, or `Menubar` for an app menu bar | `navigation-menu`, `menubar` |
  | app shell navigation column | `Sidebar` | `sidebar` |
  | hand-rolled tab list | `Tabs`, `TabsList`, `TabsTrigger`, `TabsContent` | `tabs` |
  | hand-rolled dropdown | `DropdownMenu` | `dropdown-menu` |
  | right-click menu | `ContextMenu` | `context-menu` |
  | hover-triggered tooltip | `Tooltip` | `tooltip` |
  | hover-triggered rich preview | `HoverCard` | `hover-card` |
  | click-triggered floating panel | `Popover` | `popover` |
  | a toggleable icon button | `Toggle`, `ToggleGroup` | `toggle`, `toggle-group` |
  | an inline notice or warning box | `Alert` | `alert` |
  | a transient notification | `toast` from `sonner` | `sonner` |
  | `overflow-auto` div with custom scrollbars | `ScrollArea` | `scroll-area` |
  | grey loading placeholder div | `Skeleton` | `skeleton` |
  | a spinning loader | `Spinner` | `spinner` |
  | "nothing here yet" state | `Empty` | `empty` |
  | a repeated list row of icon + text + action | `Item` | `item` |

  **No raw-HTML equivalent — use these rather than hand-rolling:** `Carousel` (`carousel`), `Chart` + `ChartContainer`/`ChartTooltip` (`chart`), `Command` for a command palette or search list (`command`), `Resizable` for draggable panes (`resizable`), `Calendar` for any month grid (`calendar`).

  **Composed patterns, not single files** — do not try to import these; build them from the parts: **Combobox** = `Command` inside `Popover`. **Date picker** = `Calendar` inside `Popover`. **Data table** = `Table` plus TanStack Table.

  Two caveats. The registry moves: `Empty`, `Field`, `Item`, `Kbd`, `Spinner`, `ButtonGroup` and `InputGroup` are recent additions — confirm the file exists in `src/components/ui/` before importing, since a block that imports a component the buyer has not installed fails **13.8**. And `toast` now ships as `sonner`; the old `toast`/`use-toast` pair is deprecated
- [ ] **3.11** **Review the whole hierarchy, not the diff** — inspect the entire component for reuse opportunities even when only one line was changed: duplicated JSX to componentize, hand-rolled markup that an existing primitive already covers, deeply nested structures to flatten
- [ ] **3.12** **Stable `key` on every list item** — anything rendered from `.map()` carries a `key` taken from the data's own identity (`user.id`), never the array index and never omitted
- [ ] **3.13** **Inline `<svg>` markup is pulled out of the JSX (CRITICAL)** — a raw `<svg>...</svg>` block never sits inline in the returned JSX, no matter how small. Extract it as its own **normal `function` declaration above the main component**, named for what it renders, and call it like any other element. Follows the same placement as **3.9**:

  ```tsx
  function CheckmarkIcon() {
    return (
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" className="size-4">
        <path d="..." />
      </svg>
    )
  }

  export default function PricingCard() {
    return (
      <div>
        <CheckmarkIcon />
        <span>Included</span>
      </div>
    )
  }
  ```

  ```tsx
  // ❌ Wrong — svg left inline in the returned JSX
  export default function PricingCard() {
    return (
      <div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" className="size-4">
          <path d="..." />
        </svg>
        <span>Included</span>
      </div>
    )
  }
  ```

  A repeated inline `<svg>` compounds both **3.9** (duplicated JSX) and this check — extract it once, reuse the function. Icons already available from `lucide-react` or `@tabler/icons-react` should use those instead of hand-rolled markup at all.

  **An SVG encoded as a `data:` URI inside `className` is the same violation in a worse form.** A noise texture or pattern written as `bg-[url('data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg…')]` puts several hundred percent-encoded characters into a class string, where it cannot be read, diffed, or edited, and where `prettier` will not wrap it. Extract the SVG to a function and render it as a positioned element, exactly as above.

