The summary is only emitted once the **Convergence Loop** reaches its stop condition — a full iteration with zero ❌. "Fixed During Review" is a history of what earlier iterations caught and repaired, not a list of open failures; at emission time there are none. Emit `🔴 FAIL — could not converge after N iterations` only if the loop is genuinely stuck (the same check keeps failing after being "fixed", or a fix is blocked by something outside the file) — never as a substitute for finishing the loop.
